Z||000009||mblackwell||05-23-2001||02:56 PM||||I had a dream once that my Fiero was equipped with the washing machine option.  there was a hidden zipper under the passenger seat.  You jammed clothes in there, drove around, and they would end up coming out of a hidden door behind the rear licence plate.  The you hung them on the spoiler to dry them.<P>Analyze that one!<P>Yes, I am insane.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||05-23-2001||03:45 PM||||My father died when I was 23, and had a closed casket funeral, so I never saw his body.<P>  A few years later I had a dream I was walking by his house and he was sitting on the porch, just like always.<P>  I went up to him and said, you cant be here, you died 4 years ago, and we sold your house to someone else! You cant be here!<P>  He said he had been doing secret work for the government, and they had to fake his death - but it was all over now so he was back.<P>  I said, but we sold your house to someone!<P>   and he said, yeah, the government bought it back for me, and replaced all my stuff.<P>   It was so realistic, and it seemed plausible at the time. I woke up and sat up in bed and was just like Ted Theodore Logan, "WHOA!!!!!!!"<P>  Its totally amazing how your mind runs in back burner mode to try and come up with ideas and solutions to problems and situations that you would never think up on your own.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroLisa||05-23-2001||03:48 PM||||in Psych class today, I learned about how according to Freud, your dreams are just a release to your unconscious feelings and desires: things like not ever seeing the body of your father, you never consciously realized what an effect that had.||||reg||1
