Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||05-23-2001||04:39 PM||||A death in the family is such an emotional shock that is hard to really belive that the person is gone - that is a big part of why we have funerals with the person lying in the casket for 2 or 3 days, so your subconscience mind will absorb the fact that your loved one is really dead.<P>  My brother in law died in a plane crash in alaska, and was never found. His 4 year old son secretly believed his father wasnt really dead - same situation, never got to actually see his dead body. He had trouble for years until he finally accepted the fact that his dad really was gone.<P>  funerals are weird when you think about it - but they do play a very important role in the greiving process.||||reg||1
